k but forfeit the opportunity to gain free material and leave White with a development advantage. \n- g7 is slightly active but risks future exposure; h8/f8 are passive retreats.\n\nReason: Capturing the bishop is the only move that converts the defensive necessity into a decisive material gain. The position after capture leaves Black a piece up with no vulnerabilities, maximizing winning chances.\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e6"}
